Prefab changes (on your Card prefab):

On the root Card GameObject itself (the one with RectTransform, Card, CardDrag, CardHover, BoxCollider2D) — 
add an Image component. Source Image = None, Color alpha = 0, Raycast Target ✓. This becomes the stationary hit-target for UI hover, 
same size as the card's own RectTransform, same idea as your fixed-size BoxCollider2D but for the UI raycaster instead of Physics2D.
Under visual, uncheck Raycast Target on: Image (cardImage), EdgeImage (cardEdgeImage), and the four TMP labels — cardName, cardNumber, 
price, cardDescript. Looking at your prefab YAML, those TMP labels currently have m_RaycastTarget: 1, which was almost certainly 
contributing to the flicker too, since text bounding boxes count as raycast surfaces. The new Awake() code will force all of these to false at runtime regardless, 
but fixing it in the prefab makes it correct in the editor too rather than relying purely on a runtime patch.
